reviews.body:
I think it would make sense to get this PR into a state where it can serve as a concrete proposal for the discussion in London, rather than having several versions of the text scattered across the list.

My suggestion for this would be to update it to reflect @TimidRobot 's 7 August redraft: "inference" defined once in Section 2, symmetric "directed by system" / "directed by user" naming, and the "or any other mechanism that is not a human user" catch so nothing falls between the two categories. 

That version also picks up @sposth 's point that the distinction turns on who identifies the asset, which I think is right. I personally have no attachment to the wording @natehake and I originally proposed and I think this redraft answers Sebastian's naming objection and @coopdanger 's Section 2 point better than what we originally proposed. 

@TimidRobot are you ok with this?
@martinthomson does this approach make sense to you? 
@natehake since the branch is yours, I assume it's easiest if you push the update?
